osed_at":"2025-09-23T21:31:12Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n4.5.stable, 4.4.1.stable\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.stable - Windows 11 (build 26100) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4070 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.8115) - 12th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-12600K (16 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhile NVIDIA Smooth Motion is enabled, running the game results in the framerate being capped at 50% of the currently used screen's max refresh rate. (30 FPS for my 60Hz monitor & 83 FPS for my 165Hz monitor). \n\nWith Smooth Motion disabled, the framerate remains unaffected, no matter on which monitor the game is being displayed.\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4cb7d593-7770-4745-b535-62b35a73f414\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Enable Smooth Motion in NVIDIA Control Panel\n2. Run any Godot project\n3. Observable maximum framerate is being capped at 50% of the currently used screen's max refresh rate\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[smooth motion mrp.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/22498802/smooth.motion.mrp.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"DeltateeDev","id":115371940,"node_id":"U_kgDOBuBvpA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/115371940?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeltateeDev","html_url":"https://github.com/DeltateeDev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeltateeDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeltateeDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeltateeDev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeltateeDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delta